    {
      "id": "node_afca91af-9db7-4648-894e-948214e6b2d8",
      "name": "router",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "link_66e6e8e4-5fb1-4171-8bc9-1d22a4323ec5"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "cfd0b99d-078f-42a7-8a14-c4a6fe1ad098",
        "link_1a170b1e-0115-44b9-9440-78eac48c77ce",
        "link_7392aa1b-0044-4e3a-a41b-84063ff15470",
        "link_ea685463-77d8-4af7-87d0-b4b485ff73bc"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": -58.302269072193425,
        "y": 943.3030217355443,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 138.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 138.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 138.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
      "text": {
        "source": "while (request.length > 0) {\n  const item = request.shift();\n  let route = routeNotFoundRequest;\n  // The request line's first two words, as sscanf(\"%7s %255s\") reads them.\n  const [method, target] = item.request.header.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n  if (target !== undefined && (method === \"GET\" || method === \"HEAD\")) {\n    switch (target.slice(0, 255).split(\"?\")[0]) {\n      case \"/home/about\": route = routeHomeAboutRequest; break;\n      case \"/home/version\": route = routeHomeVersionRequest; break;\n      case \"/api/user\": route = routeApiUserDetailsRequest; break;\n    }\n  }\n  route.push(item);\n}",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Dispatches each request to exactly one route.\n\nPop every ReqRep from `request`, read the request line \"<METHOD> <path> HTTP/x.y\" from\nrequest.header and strip any query string from the path. GET or HEAD for /home/about,\n/home/version or /api/user go to the matching route*Request link; everything else\n(other methods, unknown paths, unparsable request lines) goes to routeNotFoundRequest.\nThe router only borrows the request strings and never builds a response.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- \"GET /home/about?lang=en\" reaches routeHomeAbout.\n- \"POST /home/about\" and \"GET /nowhere\" reach routeNotFound.\n- A header without a request line reaches routeNotFound.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
      "binaryContent": null,
      "technology": {
